# The trimmed GStreamer runtime, one directory per platform, is build output
# and never source. It is eighty to a hundred megabytes and it is different on
# every machine, so it is made rather than committed:
#
#   dev/bundle-gstreamer.sh          on macOS and Linux
#   dev\bundle-gstreamer.ps1         on Windows
#
# tauri.conf.json lists gstreamer/ under bundle.resources, so whatever is here
# when `cargo tauri build` runs goes inside the app, and the shell finds it at
# resource_dir()/gstreamer. With nothing here the app falls back to the
# GStreamer installed on the machine, which is how a developer build works.
macos/
windows/
linux/
!.gitignore
